{# DRAFT 3 — permitted reasons
   PLACEHOLDERS: followerInterruption and nonFollowerInterruption are proposed
   integer settings. Replace these field names with the actual decorators.
#}
[ system ]
{% set ss = get_speaker_selector_settings() %}
{% set followerInterruption = default(ss.followerInterruption, 3) %}
{% set nonFollowerInterruption = default(ss.nonFollowerInterruption, 2) %}
{% set tagEngaged = ss.tagEngaged %}
{% set tagInScene = ss.tagInScene %}

{% set hasExchange = existsIn(lastSpeaker, "name") and existsIn(lastDialogueTarget, "name") %}
{% set playerSpoke = hasExchange and lastSpeaker.UUID == player.UUID %}
{% set playerWasAddressed = hasExchange and lastDialogueTarget.UUID == player.UUID %}
{% set playerNonFollowerExchange = false %}
{% if playerSpoke and not is_follower(lastDialogueTarget.UUID) %}
{% set playerNonFollowerExchange = true %}
{% elif playerWasAddressed and not is_follower(lastSpeaker.UUID) %}
{% set playerNonFollowerExchange = true %}
{% endif %}

# Reaction selection

{{ lastSpeaker.name }} has completed a line to {{ lastDialogueTarget.name }}.

Return exactly:

- `0` if no NPC speaks; or
- `[exact candidate name]>[exact target]`

No other text is allowed.

# Eligible speakers

The following people can be eligible:

1. The NPC marked `[RECIPIENT]`, because they were addressed.
2. Another candidate only when at least one reason printed for that candidate's class below clearly applies to the completed line.

The following are never reasons to speak: proximity, an ordinary pause, follower status, `[ENGAGED]`, or the player taking time to answer.

Never select `[PREVIOUS SPEAKER]`.

{% if playerNonFollowerExchange %}
# Permitted reasons for a follower to enter this exchange

{% if followerInterruption == 1 %}
None. A follower cannot be selected.
{% elif followerInterruption == 2 %}
- The completed line addressed or referred to this follower.
- This follower's role requires a response in this exchange.
- This follower's Interjection text names a specific friend, family member, lover, or rival discussed in the completed line.
{% elif followerInterruption == 3 %}
- The completed line addressed or referred to this follower.
- This follower's role requires a response in this exchange.
- Any specific item in this follower's Interjection text clearly matches the completed line.
- This follower has a role-based or Interjection-based reason to enter an actual argument, threat, or fight.
{% elif followerInterruption == 4 %}
- Any reason allowed at the previous position.
- Recent events show a decision that directly affects this follower.
- This follower's supplied profile gives a reason tied specifically to the completed line.
{% else %}
Judge from the recent dialogue and all supplied character information whether this follower would characteristically enter now. Require a reason tied to this exchange; presence and follower status remain insufficient.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% if hasExchange %}
# Permitted reasons for an unrelated non-follower to enter this exchange

The `[RECIPIENT]` is not an unrelated non-follower.

{% if nonFollowerInterruption == 1 %}
None. An unrelated non-follower cannot be selected.
{% elif nonFollowerInterruption == 2 %}
- The completed line addressed or referred to this person.
- This person's role requires a response in this exchange.
- This person's Interjection text names a specific person discussed in the completed line.
{% elif nonFollowerInterruption == 3 %}
- The completed line addressed or referred to this person.
- This person's role requires a response in this exchange.
- Any specific item in this person's Interjection text clearly matches the completed line.
- This person has a role-based or Interjection-based reason to enter an actual argument, threat, or fight.
{% else %}
- Any reason allowed at the previous position.
- This person's supplied profile gives a reason tied specifically to the completed line.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

# Selection

- If the `[RECIPIENT]` is an NPC candidate and a response follows naturally, prefer that candidate.
- If the recipient is the player, prefer `0` unless another candidate has a permitted reason strong enough to interrupt.
- A candidate with no permitted reason is ineligible even if their dialogue might be entertaining.
- When more than one candidate is eligible, select the one whose reason is most specific to the completed line.
- If nobody is eligible, select `0`.

# Virtual NPC restrictions

- A regular NPC cannot hear or answer a Virtual NPC.
- A regular NPC cannot target a Virtual NPC.
- A Virtual NPC may target another Virtual NPC.

{{ get_scene_context(0, 0, "full") }}
[ end system ]

[ user ]
